title: 'statement-store: keep light peers out of the DHT index on identify'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    On the v2 DHT path a light peer no longer enters the DHT index through identify. The topology
    marks a peer as light once its statement handshake shows the light role, and identify skips a
    marked peer. Before, identify indexed every peer that announced the statement protocol, so
    light clients counted as storage replicas, and a full node treated most new statements as
    transient.
crates:
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: patch
